    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d624-a2">

                <pb facs="0539" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg423"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs</hi>.</head>
                <p>Referring to my note No. 167. The Government of Ecuador desires to negotiate a
                    convention giving the U. S. the right to make whatever municipal and sanitary
                    regulations may be necessary for stamping out yellow fever and bubonic plague in
                    the port of Guayaquil. It is understood that this convention does not refer to
                    and does not consider any permanent public works, the construction of which may
                    be postponed to a later date and provided for in a manner most agreeable to the
                    Government of Ecuador.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February
                                5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. R. Tobar</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
